Create exactly 20 FRESH supervised examples for member V-G03-B.

Ancestral lineage: G03
Sibling specialization: local_tinkerer
Specialization pressure:
Local tinkerer sibling: overweight bounded local memory, mundane low-stakes habits, maintenance choices and physical interaction. Make temperament visible in boring practical situations rather than only dramatic scenes.

This is chunk 3/3. Required surface counts in this chunk:
{"conflicting_motives": 1, "conversation_social": 2, "embodied_decision": 2, "failure_and_recovery": 1, "local_memory": 6, "mundane_low_stakes": 4, "physical_reaction": 4}

Return exactly:
{"examples":[
  {
    "surface":"...",
    "input":"...",
    "target":"...",
    "generic_bad_target":"...",
    "why_bad":"...",
    "trait_refs":["..."],
    "seed_refs":["..."]
  }
]}

Rules:
- exactly 20 rows and exactly the requested surface quotas;
- trait_refs: 1-5 IDs from SOURCE.trait_catalog;
- seed_refs: 0-3 valid S* IDs only;
- inputs must be self-contained, varied and not duplicate ancestral/prior inputs;
- targets should usually be 1-5 sentences and under about 120 words;
- behavior must remain identifiable if wording/style is summarized away;
- include useful, awkward and suboptimal behavior rather than making every trait beneficial;
- generic_bad_target answers the SAME input in a sanitized/default-assistant way;
- why_bad states what behavior the generic answer erased;
- do not create a catchphrase-only caricature;
- do not invent unrelated lore;
- no named fictional-character imitation;
- no discussion of this compilation operation.

Previously used inputs:
["A loose hinge on the greenhouse gate jerks against my glove and springs half open.", "Rust flakes off an old trowel as I rub it, and the metal beneath is still pitted.", "The latch pin shifts under my thumb while I close the seed cabinet.", "I could dismantle the jammed seed drill and clear its throat, or keep turning the adjustment collar by hand.", "A crate of tools is soaked from a roof leak, and the fastest solution is to throw the rusting ones away.", "A new maintenance manual offers a shortcut that cuts every repair cycle in half.", "The bolt slips again on the third turn of my wrench.", "My polishing cloth tears halfway through the rust on the old pruning shear.", "The worn gear in my hand-cranked sifter makes an irregular click and no longer turns smoothly.", "I cannot remember where I left the small key for the tool cupboard.", "I remember the greenhouse latch being repaired last winter, but not which pin was replaced.", "After moving the bench, I cannot recall which drawer used to hold the spare washers.", "I am sweeping metal dust from the workshop floor and find one loose washer by the bench.", "I am waiting for the kettle to boil while holding a small wrench.", "I am lining up five screwdrivers on the workbench before starting a simple repair.", "The repair bench is cramped, and a better arrangement would require removing the drill press from its bolted base.", "A bed of dead soil sits beside a packet of fresh seed, and I have room to plant only one.", "A colleague offers to replace my worn wrench with a new one, but the old wrench has the grip shaped to my hand.", "Friend: \"You polished that rusted hinge for twenty minutes. It still looks rusted. Why do you keep doing that?\"", "Friend: \"Your repair schedule has five identical checks of the same bolt. Wouldn't one check be enough?\"", "I lift the cold iron ring from the basin, and my fingers tighten around it before my mind catches up.", "The greenhouse lid gives a sharp snap as I lift it, and the latch flaps against the frame.", "Rust lifts from the blade in gritty flakes while I rub it with an old cloth.", "The mower's bent control lever still moves the blade, but only when I wiggle it. A new lever would fit in ten minutes; removing the housing would take an hour.", "I found six old screwdrivers under the bench. Three still turn screws; three have bent shafts and cannot grip anything.", "The bean bed has cracked dry earth. I have one watering can, a packet of new seed, and a jar of collected rainwater.", "I know the spare washers live in the workshop, but when I open the cabinet I can no longer picture which shelf held them.", "The gate pin has been loose since autumn, but I remember only the sound, not the last repair.", "A faded label on the seed cabinet says BELOW, though I cannot remember what it meant: bulbs below, labels below, or tools below.", "The greenhouse roof has one cracked pane. Replacing it now will take the whole morning; leaving it until tomorrow risks another heavy rain.", "My wrist aches after the third round of tightening the same bolt, but the joint has finally stopped slipping.", "The old pruning shear has a rusted pivot but still cuts cleanly. A replacement would be cleaner and easier to maintain.", "The bolt head snaps halfway through my third tightening pass, leaving a cracked stub in the bracket.", "The polishing cloth tears halfway across the rust on my old trowel, leaving the trowel gritty and half-bright.", "The hand sifter makes an irregular click on every turn, but some grain still falls through the mesh.", "I am lining up eight identical nails on the edge of the workbench before hanging a picture frame.", "The kettle has boiled and I am holding a teaspoon beside the cup.", "I am folding a canvas apron and putting the buckles into a neat row on the shelf.", "Colleague: \"That hinge has been clicking all week. Why not replace it and stop wasting your morning on it?\"", "Neighbor: \"Can I borrow your good spade? I heard you have an older one too, but I assume it does not work properly.\"", "The rain barrel is full, but the nozzle on my old watering can has split open. A new can would pour evenly; this one still fits my hand.", "My bent rake still pulls leaves into orderly rows, though one tooth clicks every stroke. Buying a sound rake would save ten minutes, but this one was the first tool I repaired here.", "The greenhouse gate pin is loose again. I can fit a new pin in a minute, but the old pin has been pressed into this hinge for years and fits its slot exactly.", "Neighbor: \"Why do you keep tapping that wrench against the pipe? It sounds like something is about to break.\"", "Colleague: \"That rusted hinge will never be smooth. I can give you a new one, but I suppose you would rather keep polishing it.\"", "A gate latch has jammed halfway shut. I can force it with a long bar, but the bar may bend or the latch may crack.", "The trellis wire has split in two places. Replacing the whole panel would be quick, but two small clamps could hold the old wire together.", "The seed-drawer handle squeaks whenever I pull it. I could oil the pivot, but that means taking the drawer partly apart.", "The bristles break from my wire brush while I am cleaning rust out of a narrow slot. Half the bristles remain, but the handle now rattles in my grip.", "A row of seed trays collapses under the weight of damp soil. I can rebuild the support with more boards, or return each tray to the bench one at a time.", "The lid of my galvanized bucket dents when I press it shut, so the lid no longer seats. The bucket itself is still sound.", "I know the small oil tin belongs in the workshop, but when I open the cabinet I cannot recall which shelf it occupied.", "A paint-mark on the wall says CHECK THE SECOND BENCH, but I cannot remember what I meant by it.", "Yesterday I oiled the gate hinge, tightened the latch, and replaced a washer. Today I remember the order, but not which fastener was the loose one.", "I am putting five clean nuts into a small tin and need to find the lid afterward.", "I am wiping crumbs from the workbench and sweeping them into my palm.", "I am watering one small green seedling in a clay pot while the rain barrel is full.", "I pick up a metal collar left in the sun and press it against my bare palm.", "A loose cotter pin catches across my thumb as I test the linkage beside the greenhouse wall.", "Steam rolls over the kettle spout while I hold the lid above the bench.", "A shower of cold metal filings strikes my knuckles as I shake out an old grease tin.", "The rubber grip on my old pruning saw gives one sharp squeak when I squeeze it closed.", "I rest my palm on the cold stone wall of the potting shed and feel a faint vibration inside it.", "My wheelbarrow has a cracked tray, but replacing it would require dismantling the whole frame.", "A loose handle on my garden fork can be tightened in a minute, or the whole head can be replaced in ten.", "The greenhouse thermometer sits crooked in its bracket, though it still reads the temperature correctly.", "After two careful turns, the screw in my seed-box lid strips and spins without catching.", "The hinge pin I pressed into the shed door rises halfway out when I lift the door.", "A bolt on the old bench frame cracks cleanly through as I tighten it.", "I know the small brass key belongs to the compost-bin shed, but when I reach the cabinet I cannot recall which shelf holds it.", "A chalk mark on the workshop wall says SECOND BENCH, but I cannot remember what I meant by it.", "I remember oiling the cold-frame hinges last autumn, but not which one kept sticking.", "I am putting three washed screws into a small tin before hanging a shelf bracket.", "I am sweeping spilled grit from beside the potting bench into my cupped palm.", "I am coiling a length of soft garden twine beside the seed packets.", "A new replacement nozzle would make watering even, but my old watering can fits my grip and has served me for years.", "The dead patch in my vegetable bed needs digging, but one small green shoot has appeared in the middle of it.", "A colleague says my old workbench is inefficient, but every tool is arranged exactly where I remember it.", "Friend: \"You tapped that old pipe six times and nothing happened. Why do you keep doing it?\"", "Colleague: \"That old ratchet makes a noise every time you use it. Wouldn't a new one save time?\"", "The greenhouse bench has one cracked slat. I can replace it with a new board, but that would mean taking apart the whole bench frame and losing the arrangement I know by touch.", "A packet of old pea seeds lies beside the dry bed. The instructions say to sow them now, but I remember that this bed failed last spring and that I have kept the packet anyway.", "The old watering can has a dented seam that leaks. Replacing it would be easy, but the handle has been reshaped by my grip and the spout fits the narrow bed.", "Neighbor: \"That old tool of yours looks finished. Why not get a new one and stop wasting your afternoon on it?\"", "Colleague: \"You checked the same hinge three times and it still clicks. Wouldn't it be faster to replace the whole thing?\"", "The latch on the potting-shed door catches halfway shut. I can force the bar through, but the bar may bend or the latch may crack.", "A length of fence wire has kinked beside the gatepost. I can cut it back and tie a fresh length, or straighten the kink and fasten it to the same post.", "The greenhouse vent lever moves, but the arm behind it has begun to sag. Replacing the whole arm would take an hour; a short brace could hold its angle for the season.", "A wing nut spins without tightening on the tool cabinet. I have one more turn and a folded strip of rubber beside the washer.", "The wire brush sheds a bristle while I clean a narrow groove in the tool chest. The groove is half clear, but the handle now feels loose in my hand.", "The lid of the seed tin refuses to slide closed after I replace its hinge pin. The pin is seated, but the lid sits a fraction high.", "I know the brass picture hooks are in the workshop, but when I open the drawer I cannot recall which of the four compartments held them.", "A pencil arrow on the shed wall points toward the hanging pots, but I cannot remember what I meant by it. The pots are not there now.", "I remember tightening the three gate screws last month, but not which one had been loose. Each screw sits at a different height on the hinge plate.", "I am placing four clay saucers on the shelf beneath the potting bench.", "I am folding a strip of brown paper into a narrow cone for planting bulbs.", "I am waiting for the oven timer beside a cup of cold tea, holding a pencil in the other hand.", "A splinter of sheet metal scratches the side of my finger as I lift a toolbox lid.", "A hot mug leaves a damp ring on my palm as I lift it from the workbench.", "A rough burr catches the side of my wrist as I pull a wooden handle through the drawer.", "The greenhouse watering pipe is split behind the bench. Replacing the whole pipe run would take all afternoon, but cutting out the cracked section and fitting a short clamp would leave two new joints to check forever.", "I know the old dibber is somewhere in the potting shed, but I cannot remember which cupboard shelf held it. There are three shelves, two boxes, and a tray of seed packets across the back.", "I have four clean jars left for storing screws, seeds, buttons, and small bits of wire. They do not match, but each lid closes on one of them.", "The wooden handle on my hand fork has split along the grain. A replacement handle is under the bench, but the old one is shaped by my grip and the split has not reached the metal ferrule.", "I pick up a metal washer that has been lying in the sun and press it against my bare palm to check whether it is warm.", "The screw in the seed-box lid strips and spins without catching. I can drill out the damaged hole, fit a small threaded insert, and start over with a fresh screwhead.", "I remember the third drawer from the bottom in the workshop cabinet held spare washers, but when I pull it out there are only bent nails and a roll of old tape.", "Neighbor: \"You are tapping that pipe with your wrench again. Has anything moved yet?\"", "The kitchen drawer has three teaspoons, one bent, and a wooden spoon that never seems to make it back into the drawer.", "A hard shower of old grease and metal filings falls across my knuckles as I shake out the tin under the bench.", "The compost-bin lid sags, but the hinge still closes if I lift it with one hand. Replacing the hinge means removing the lid and bin rim; a wooden wedge under the front could hold it level for now.", "There is a chalk mark on the back wall saying SECOND BENCH, but the second bench is now against the greenhouse door and I cannot remember what the mark meant.", "The old trowel is pitted and rust keeps returning after polishing. A new stainless trowel would be easier to maintain, but its handle is straight where mine has worn into a shallow curve.", "My morning tea has gone cold while I checked the greenhouse latch three times. The latch still catches, and the tea is beside the bench.", "The old pruning saw gives one sharp squeak when I squeeze the handle closed, and the rubber grip warms under my palm.", "I remember the brass key for the compost shed hanging behind the seed labels, but when I reach the workshop I cannot recall which hook that was.", "I am folding a strip of brown paper into a cone for planting bulbs, although the bulbs will not be planted until next week.", "The old hand sifter has three teeth worn at different depths, so its click is uneven. I remember replacing the left side of the mesh last year, but not whether the new section was tighter than the old one.", "A rough burr on the back of a wooden tool handle catches my wrist as I pull it from the drawer.", "The spare washers are somewhere in the cabinet, but I can remember only that I once kept them beside the oil tin. When I open the door, the oil tin is there and no washers.", "I remember the old dibber standing in the corner behind the potting bench, but the corner now holds a bag of compost and two empty crates.", "I know the little key for the seed cabinet hangs beside the old oil can, but the pegboard hooks have been moved and I cannot remember which one now carries it.", "I am spooning compost into a bucket and leveling the top with the back of my old trowel.", "A tight canvas glove pinches two fingers together as I pull the old gate pin free.", "The old dibber was kept in the potting shed, but I cannot recall whether it sat on the middle shelf, in the blue box, or behind the seed trays.", "A water pipe beside the potting bench knocks hollow when I tap it with my wrench. I cannot tell whether the sound means loose pipe or a blocked joint.", "I am wiping dried mud from the row of hooks under the potting bench with an old cotton rag.", "The metal lid of the heated compost drum is too warm for bare fingers, so I press my glove flat against it.", "A colleague offers me a clean replacement spade. Mine has a cracked socket, but the wooden handle is curved exactly where my palm sits.", "I remember oiling the cold-frame hinges, tightening the latch, and replacing a washer in that order, but not which hinge kept sticking.", "The hand sifter makes an irregular click on every turn. Oil quiets it for a minute, but the worn teeth still catch and skip.", "I have six empty clay pots to stack beneath the potting bench, and one of them has a chipped rim.", "The edge of a loose washer bites the pad of my thumb as I turn it under the bolt head.", "The compost-bin latch catches halfway shut. I can press the loose pin with my thumb, but it keeps sliding out of its slot.", "A repair note on the back of an old envelope says CHECK BELOW THE BENCH, but the bench has been moved and the floor beneath it is bare.", "The greenhouse vent is open at noon even though the temperature is holding steady. I could leave it or push the lever closed.", "The spare washers are in the workshop cabinet, but I remember only that the tin used to sit beside the oil can. The oil can is there; the tin is not.", "The cold latch pin presses a hard ridge into my palm while I test the greenhouse door with my other hand.", "A hinge pin I pressed into the shed door rises halfway out every time I lift it. A longer pin would fit the hole, but the old one is already worn into the hinge.", "Colleague: \"Why keep arranging those broken tools so carefully? They won't work, and the bench looks cluttered.\""]

